MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Covers BranchController, ProductController, ProductPrintConfigController,
PrintersController, PrintImagesController (29 endpoints).

- Add Swagger/Examples/BranchExamples.cs, ProductExamples.cs,
  ProductPrintConfigExamples.cs, PrintersExamples.cs,
  PrintImagesExamples.cs and register them in ExampleCatalog.
- Backfill missing <response> XML doc tags on all 29 actions (same
  gap flagged, but only partly closed, in S1).
- Continue the 401/403 accuracy audit from S1, with the opposite
  finding this time: the Printing module's admin-only writes enforce
  'system-admin only' in the service (Forbidden category), not via an
  authorization policy, so their 403 genuinely IS the enveloped
  ApiResponse<T> body — documented explicitly, contrasted with
  TenantsController's policy-driven empty-body 403 from S1.
  BranchController/ProductController similarly have a rare
  enveloped-401 edge case (ActorNotResolved) reachable from
  Create/Delete/Restore.
- Document PrintImagesController.Upload's 409: uniquely a SUCCESS
  envelope (existing image's metadata) with status forced to 409, not
  an ApiError — the only non-2xx-without-ApiError response found so
  far.
- Update Docs/PROJECT_KNOWLEDGE.md (§3, §18, metadata trailer) with
  S2 coverage and both new findings.

Remaining controllers land in S3 (Stock/ProductItems/Inventory
upload/InventoryHistory/CardFiles), S4 (Transactions/CardDisposals),
S5 (BranchRequests).
